55
00:53:50.000 --> 00:54:56.000
If police could not solve the murder fairly, then they would do it unfairly. Yes, ladies and gentlemen, the defense calls the police liars. They pointed out that the interview in which Beatty allegedly confessed had not been recorded as others had been. The prosecution stated that if the police had indeed fabricated the confession, then they were such talented actors that they should be members of the Royal Shakespeare Company. They asserted that Beatty had broken down on the stand because he was haunted by his guilt. Before the jury was dismissed for deliberations, judge Lord Thomas Dawson made it clear to them that their verdict hinged on Beatty's alleged confession. He said, Either the police officers are lying, or the accused is not telling us the truth.
如果警方无法公正地破获这起谋杀案，那么他们就会用不公正的手段来做。是的，女士们先生们，辩方称警察是骗子。他们指出，贝蒂据称招供的讯问并没有像其他讯问那样被录音。控方表示，如果警方确实捏造了供词，那么他们就是如此有天赋的演员，应该去皇家莎士比亚剧团。他们断言，贝蒂在证人席上崩溃是因为他被内疚折磨。在陪审团休庭退席进行商议之前，法官托马斯·道森勋爵向他们明确指出，他们的裁决取决于贝蒂所谓的供词。他说：“要么是警官在撒谎，要么是被告没有对我们说实话。”

56
00:54:56.000 --> 00:55:53.000
The jury returned with a verdict that same day. They found Brian Beatty guilty of the murder of Lawrence Haggart and of fire-raising. The courtroom erupted in cheers and applause. In addressing Beatty, judge Dawson described his unprovoked attack brutal and ferocious. He added that Beatty's criminal history was very serious and he was an extreme danger to the public. Judge Dawson sentenced Beatty to life in prison with a minimum of 15 years. His sentence for fire-raising would run concurrently with his sentence for murder. Larry Haggart was grateful to those who conducted the renewed investigation into his son's murder.
陪审团当天就做出了裁决。他们裁定布赖恩·贝蒂谋杀劳伦斯·哈格特和纵火罪名成立。法庭爆发出一阵欢呼和掌声。道森法官在对贝蒂讲话时，将他的无端袭击描述为残酷而凶猛的。他补充说，贝蒂的犯罪史非常严重，对公众构成了极端的危险。道森法官判处贝蒂无期徒刑，至少服刑15年。他的纵火罪刑期将与谋杀罪刑期同时执行。拉里·哈格特对那些对儿子谋杀案进行重新调查的人表示感谢。

57
00:55:53.000 --> 00:57:11.000
Yet he remained angry that it had taken more than two years to identify and convict Lawrence's killer. He accused Scotland police of botching the investigation by failing to verify Beatty's alibi and for not singling him out as a likely suspect based on his criminal history. Larry also stated that by focusing on Dennis as the perpetrator, the police had given Beatty a plan of defence. In the aftermath of the trial, the Haggart family lodged a civil complaint against central Scotland police. It addressed the investigation team's mishandling of the case and their poor conduct towards the Haggarts, including the persistent and baseless pursuit of Dennis as the killer. Dennis and John Haggart were awarded £20,000 in compensation. The police issued a public apology stating that the family should have received a much better performance. They were assured that the force had rectified its approach so that the same mistakes wouldn't be repeated.
然而，对于花了两多年时间才识别并定罪劳伦斯的凶手，他依然感到愤怒。他指责苏格兰警方搞砸了调查，未能核实贝蒂的不在场证明，也没有根据他的犯罪记录将他挑出来作为可能的嫌疑人。拉里还表示，通过将注意力集中在丹尼斯身上作为肇事者，警方给了贝蒂一个辩护方案。审判结束后，哈格特家族对中苏格兰警方提起了一起民事诉讼。诉讼内容涉及调查小组对案件的处理不当以及对哈格特一家的恶劣态度，包括对丹尼斯作为凶手持续且毫无根据的追查。丹尼斯和约翰·哈格特获得了2万英镑的赔偿金。警方发表公开道歉，称该家属本应得到好得多的对待。他们被保证该部队已经纠正了其方法，以便不会重复同样的错误。

58
00:57:11.000 --> 00:58:27.000
Larry Haggart told BBC Scotland that he welcomed the apology, but he wanted the officers involved sacked. The mayhem they caused to the family, especially the two boys. To me, they've got off too lightly. In mid-1998, an independent inquiry was held to determine what exactly went wrong in central Scotland police's initial investigation into Lawrence Haggart's murder. Conducting the inquiry was Assistant Chief Constable James Mackay of the Tayside Police. His findings were published three months later in a document dubbed The Mackay Report. The details and outcome of the report were withheld from the public, including the Haggart family. Journalist Russell Finlay had covered the case extensively for the Sunday Mail and was intrigued as to why the report had been suppressed. But there was no avenue for him or anyone else to gain access to it.
拉里·哈格特告诉英国广播公司苏格兰频道，他欢迎道歉，但他希望涉案警官被解雇。他们给这个家庭带来的混乱，尤其是两个男孩。对我说，他们逃脱得太轻松了。1998年中期，进行了一项独立调查，以确定中苏格兰警方对劳伦斯·哈格特谋杀案的最初调查到底出了什么问题。负责调查的是泰赛德警局的助理警察总长詹姆斯·麦凯。他的调查结果在三个月后发表在一份被称为《麦凯报告》的文件中。该报告的细节和结果对公众保密，包括哈格特家族。记者罗素·芬利曾为《星期日邮报》对该案进行了广泛的报道，并对该报告被压制的原因感到好奇。但没有途径让他或任何人获取它。

59
00:58:27.000 --> 00:59:39.000
Seven years later, in 2005, British Prime Minister Tony Blair passed the UK's Freedom of Information Act. This allowed members of the public to request access to information held by public authorities. Russell Finlay later wrote in his book, Acid Attack, a journalist's war with organised crime. I decided to seek a copy of the Haggart Report, so I approached Lawrence's dad Larry and submitted an application on his behalf. When it arrived, it made my blood run cold. The report revealed that in 1994, while serving time for abducting a teenage boy, Brian Beatty said he wished he'd killed his victim so that he could have escaped arrest. Social workers warned that Beatty was at high risk of reoffending, but he was released early on parole. By 1996, he had faded back into the Falkirk community.
七年后的2005年，英国首相托尼·布莱尔通过了英国的《信息自由法》。这允许公众申请获取公共机构掌握的信息。罗素·芬利后来在他的书《酸液袭击：记者与有组织犯罪的战争》中写道：“我决定寻找一份《哈格特报告》的副本，所以我找到了劳伦斯的父亲拉里，并代表他提交了申请。当它到达时，让我不寒而栗。”报告显示，1994年，布赖恩·贝蒂在因绑架一名十几岁的男孩服刑期间，曾表示他希望自己杀死了受害者，这样他就可以逃避逮捕。社会工作者警告说，贝蒂再次犯罪的风险很高，但他却提前获得假释出狱。到1996年，他又重新融入了法尔克拉克的社区。

60
00:59:39.000 --> 01:00:33.000
Then, he was questioned in relation to the Lawrence Haggart case. The police accepted his alibi and he was promptly ruled out. The Mackay report confirmed that no effort was made to verify Beatty's whereabouts on the night of Lawrence's attack. Additionally, Beatty's criminal record wasn't accessed by investigators until almost a year later. It also noted that they didn't consider that the crime could have been sexually motivated. Furthermore, two officers had searched Beatty's car and caravan following the attack. They discovered a hammer and a petrol container, but disregarded them. In one of Beatty's previous attacks, he had struck a victim over the head with a glass bottle.
然后，他因劳伦斯·哈格特案受到讯问。警方接受了他的不在场证明，并迅速排除了他的嫌疑。麦凯报告证实，警方没有做出任何努力去核实贝蒂在劳伦斯遇袭当晚的行踪。此外，调查人员直到将近一年后才查阅贝蒂的犯罪记录。它还指出，他们没有考虑到这起犯罪可能具有性动机。此外，袭击发生后，两名警察搜查了贝蒂的汽车和大篷车。他们发现了一把锤子和一个汽油桶，但却置之不理。在贝蒂以前的一次袭击中，他曾用玻璃瓶击打受害者的头部。

61
01:00:33.000 --> 01:01:48.000
A glass bottle was found in the Haggart's kitchen, but wasn't flagged as significant. Another potential weapon went missing when a piece of green metal was collected from the home, but never logged as evidence. The report detailed how fire investigators had examined the living room for 90 minutes immediately after the attack. This was before the area was secured and examined for crucial evidence such as finger or footprints. Then there was the discovery that detectives had faked a diary entries in relation to their investigation. The fraudulent entries were exposed by the author's habit of referring to Lawrence as the deceased prior to his actual death. The report also addressed confusion surrounding the discovery of a hammer in the Haggart's kitchen. One officer who inspected the property with a team of experts two days after the attack stated that if the hammer was on the kitchen table at the time, they would have seen it.
在哈格特的厨房里发现了一个玻璃瓶，但并未被标记为重要物证。当一块绿色金属从家中收集但从未被登记为证据时，另一个潜在武器消失了。报告详细描述了消防调查人员在袭击发生后立即对客厅进行了90分钟的检查。这是在现场被封锁并检查指纹或足迹等关键证据之前。然后是侦探在调查中伪造日记条目的发现。这些欺诈性条目因作者习惯在劳伦斯实际死亡之前称其为死者而被揭露。该报告还解决了围绕在哈格特厨房发现锤子的混乱情况。一名在袭击发生两天后与专家小组一起检查该房产的警官表示，如果当时锤子在厨房桌子上，他们就会看到它。

62
01:01:48.000 --> 01:02:58.000
The Haggart house was searched nine times before Detective Sergeant Robert Beveridge said he'd stumbled across the item by chance during a visit one week after the attack. The Makai report concluded that Sergeant Beveridge was lying and had planted the hammer himself. According to Assistant Chief Constable Makai, the corrupt actions of investigating officers were intended to pin the crime on 12-year-old Dennis Haggart. Sections of the report were not released to journalist Russell Finley. These included portions dealing with a criminal probe against the officers involved in the original investigation. Only a few received any disciplinary action. The case's second in command, Detective Inspector John Bunyan, was suspended in August of 1998. He faced five charges, including two counts of discredible conduct and three charges of neglect of duty.
在侦探中士罗伯特·贝弗里奇表示他在袭击发生一周后的访问中偶然发现了这件物品之前，哈格特家已经被搜查了九次。麦凯报告得出结论，贝弗里奇中士在撒谎，并且是他自己把锤子藏在那里的。据助理警察总长麦凯称，调查人员的腐败行为旨在将罪名嫁祸给12岁的丹尼斯·哈格特。报告的部分内容没有向记者罗素·芬利公布。其中包括针对最初调查中涉案警官的刑事调查部分。只有少数人受到了纪律处分。该案的第二指挥官、侦探督察约翰·邦扬于1998年8月被停职。他面临五项指控，包括两项声誉败坏的行为和三项玩忽职守的指控。

63
01:02:58.000 --> 01:04:04.000
The latter three charges were dropped after a lengthy disciplinary hearing. Inspector Bunyan was only found guilty of the two lesser offenses of discredible conduct. Detective Sergeant Robert Beveridge, the officer who planted the hammer in the Haggart's kitchen, was transferred out of the criminal investigation department, as was another sergeant. The case's former lead investigator, Detective Superintendent Jim Winning, avoided discipline by retiring from the force. Aged in his 40s, Winning cited health reasons for his early departure. Central Scotland Police had attempted to block his retirement, but were unsuccessful. Larry Haggart voiced his family's disappointment, telling the press, We have been fighting to get a bit of justice for our family for years. I just feel we haven't got it.
经过漫长的纪律听证会，后三项指控被撤销。邦扬督察仅被判定犯有两项较轻的声誉败坏罪。在哈格特厨房藏锤子的警察、侦探中士罗伯特·贝弗里奇被调离了刑事调查部门，另一名中士也是如此。该案的前首席调查员、侦探总督察吉姆·温宁通过从警队退休而避免了纪律处分。年近四十的温宁以健康为由提前离职。中苏格兰警方曾试图阻止他退休，但没有成功。拉里·哈格特表达了其家人的失望，他告诉媒体：“多年来，我们一直在为我们的家庭争取一点正义。我只是觉得我们没有得到它。”

64
01:04:04.000 --> 01:05:12.000
There is somebody answerable to the way we were treated, and as far as I'm concerned, nobody has come up with the answer yet. In 2003, Brian Beatty lost an appeal against his conviction. He was denied parole in 2012 and remains incarcerated as of the release of this episode. In October 2015, one of Beatty's nephews came forward to accuse his uncle of molesting him. Michael, not his real name, told The Sun that Beatty started abusing him in 1994, when Michael was 13 years old. He would serve Michael sugary alcoholic beverages known as Alcopops, then rape him. Michael told The Sun, quote, It was so traumatic I blocked it out. It was horrific. There were hundreds of incidents over a spell of three years.
有人必须对我们受到的对待负责，就我而言，还没有人给出答案。2003年，布赖恩·贝蒂对定罪的上诉被驳回。他在2012年被拒绝假释，截至本集发布时仍在服刑。2015年10月，贝蒂的一个侄子站出来指控他的叔叔猥亵他。迈克尔（化名）告诉《太阳报》，贝蒂在1994年开始虐待他，当时迈克尔13岁。他会给迈克尔提供被称为Alcopops的含糖酒精饮料，然后强奸他。迈克尔告诉《太阳报》：“这太创伤了，我把它屏蔽掉了。太可怕了。在三年多的时间里发生了数百起事件。”

65
01:05:12.000 --> 01:06:18.000
I would regularly wake up some days with no clothes on and him lying next to me. There were times where I'd be upstairs doing my homework, and he'd just come into my room and start doing stuff to me. Michael was scared that if he fought back, Beatty might start abusing his brothers instead. After Lawrence Haggert was murdered in March 1996, Beatty took Michael for a walk past the Haggert House. He told his nephew that he had killed Lawrence, and if Michael ever told anyone, then he would kill him as well. According to Michael, Beatty threatened his life on multiple occasions. He once held a razor to Michael's throat. Another time, he claimed to have a gun hidden under a bridge that he would use to kill him. After Beatty was convicted for murder, he sent Michael a letter.
我经常在某些日子醒来时身上没有衣服，而他躺在我旁边。有时我在楼上做作业，他就会直接走进我的房间开始对我做一些事情。迈克尔害怕如果他反击，贝蒂可能会转而虐待他的兄弟们。1996年3月劳伦斯·哈格特被谋杀后，贝蒂带着迈克尔散步经过哈格特家。他告诉侄子他杀了劳伦斯，如果迈克尔把这件事告诉任何人，他也会杀死他。据迈克尔称，贝蒂曾多次威胁他的生命。他曾把一把剃刀架在迈克尔的喉咙上。还有一次，他声称自己在一座桥下藏了一把枪，可以用它来杀死他。贝蒂因谋杀罪被定罪后，他给迈克尔写了一封信。

66
01:06:18.000 --> 01:07:13.000
In it, he said he had naked photos of Michael. He blackmailed Michael into staying silent by threatening to release the images to his friends and family. Michael became a Royal Logistics Corps soldier, but struggled with post-traumatic stress disorder, anxiety, and maintaining employment as a consequence of the abuse. His personal relationships also suffered. He told the son, He has turned me into a nervous person. I've made bad decisions and pushed away my family. My worry is now that he gets out. I think he'll try and kill me. I'm trying to move on with my life, but it's so difficult.
在信中，他说他有迈克尔的裸照。他通过威胁要将这些照片发布给他的朋友和家人来勒索迈克尔保持沉默。迈克尔成为了一名皇家后勤部队士兵，但由于虐待，他一直在与创伤后应激障碍、焦虑和保持就业作斗争。他的个人关系也受到了影响。他告诉《太阳报》：“他把我变成了一个神经质的人。我做出了糟糕的决定，并把我的家人推开。我现在的担忧是他出来。我想他会试图杀死我。我正试图继续我的生活，但这太难了。”

67
01:07:13.000 --> 01:08:11.000
In March 2016, a football tournament was held in honour of Lawrence Haggett near his hometown. More than 100 players took part. A charity auction was also held in conjunction with the event to raise funds for a local girl battling cancer. Lawrence's brother Dennis gave an interview to the Scotsman newspaper about the event. Quote, The response has been phenomenal. Thanks to social media, we have heard from people my brother played with more than 20 years ago. We've been overwhelmed by messages of support. People are just delighted to see Lawrence being remembered in this way. After Lawrence's death, his father Larry continued to be involved in football by helping to coach a youth team.
2016年3月，在他的家乡附近举办了一场为纪念劳伦斯·哈格特而举办的足球锦标赛。100多名球员参加了比赛。活动还结合举办了一场慈善拍卖会，为当地一名与癌症抗争的女孩筹集资金。劳伦斯的哥哥丹尼斯接受了《苏格兰人报》关于此次活动的采访。“反响太惊人了。多亏了社交媒体，我们收到了我哥哥20多年前一起踢球的人的消息。我们被支持的信息淹没了。人们很高兴看到劳伦斯以这种方式被人们铭记。”劳伦斯死后，他的父亲拉里继续通过帮助执教一支青年队来参与足球运动。

68
01:08:11.000 --> 01:08:16.000
He told the Herald Scotland that doing so helped with his mental health. When things got too difficult, he would rewatch home movies of Lawrence playing the sport. Larry often paused the videos at moments that reminded him of happy memories with his son. Quote, I had a lot of good times. It was short, but it was a pleasure. Thanks for watching. There aren't comments yet for this episode. Click on any sentence in the transcript to leave a comment.
他告诉《苏格兰人报》，这样做有助于他的心理健康。当事情变得太困难时，他会重新观看劳伦斯这项运动的家庭录像。拉里经常在让想起与儿子快乐回忆的时刻暂停视频。“我度过了很多美好时光。虽然短暂，但它是一种乐趣。谢谢观看。本集暂无评论。点击转录中的任何句子以发表评论。”
